  "kind": "one-step",
  "claim": "Birds on opposite edges of the torus are neighbours the short way round and are pulled together across the seam.",
  "derivation": [
    "World 20 × 20; only cohesion is on (w_c = 1). A (0.5, 10) and B (19.5, 10) both move at (0, 1).",
    "The raw offset A→B is (19, 0); the short way round is 19 − 20 = −1 (E1), so they are neighbours at distance 1 (E2).",
    "A: c = (−1, 0), |c| = 1 < 3, desired = 2.7 · (−1, 0)/3 = (−0.9, 0), so C_A = (−0.9, −1); B mirrors it with C_B = (0.9, −1) (E4).",
    "v′_A = (−0.015, 0.983333), v′_B = (0.015, 0.983333): each heads for the seam between them, not across the middle of the world (E9).",
    "x′_A = 0.5 − 0.015/60 = 0.49975 and x′_B = 19.5 + 0.015/60 = 19.50025 (E10)."
  ],
  "params": {
    "agentCount": 2, "worldWidth": 20, "worldHeight": 20,
    "separationWeight": 0, "alignmentWeight": 0, "cohesionWeight": 1,
    "perceptionRadius": 4.5, "separationRadius": 1.55,
